    "question_text": "One end of a horizontal thick copper wire of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>and radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;welded to an end of another horizontal thin copper wire of length<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> and radius<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>.&nbsp;When the arrangement stretched by applying forces at two ends, the ratio of the elongation in the thin wire to that in the thick wire is&nbsp;",
