      },
      {
        "id": "MMDzc",
        "text": "<math><mi>P</mi></math>  is more ductile than  <math><mi>Q</mi></math>",
        "image": null
      },
      {
        "id": "dWNCZ",
        "text": "<math><mi>P</mi></math>  is more brittle than  <math><mi>Q</mi></math>",
        "image": null
      },
      {
        "id": "F15GM",
        "text": "The Young's modulus of  <math><mi>P</mi></math>  is more than that of  <math><mi>Q</mi></math>",
        "image": null
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "MMDzc",
    "solution_text": "Slope of this graph represents the reciprocal of Young's modulus.<br >Since slope of <math><mi>P</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></math>  slope of Q<br >Hence Y of  <math><mi>P</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>Y</mi></math>  of Q",
    "solution_image": null,
    "topic": "Young's Modulus and Breaking Stres"
